{"_type":"shard","campaign_names":["Empire City","Roanoke S4","Roanoke Season 4 / Empire City","Season 4, Empire City","roanoke-s4"],"channel":{"category":"Ferrytown","id":"854829166561067029","name":"shop-gregarious-gauntlets🌲🛡","position":89,"server_id":"850779382791536640","topic":"This stall is run by a large bugbear man who talks in extremely dramatic fashion. Many of his pieces of armor are fancy and catching to the eye. He ages his whole lifespan over the course of a day, his taste and required gifts changing with him. The interior of the stall, which is an open-air blacksmithy with a small room in the back for sleeping, has several clocks strewn about. Unlike many of the other shops in Ferrytown which take on a different tone and goods during the night, this shop is instead closed as the bugbear begins to die at sunset and is reborn and ages enough to manage the shop by sunrise.","type":"0"},"database_path":"discord/empire-city/empire-city.sqlite","database_sha256":"a0c71f99ff403e5a91d88c2dfb647326cbc332b4b943fa207cb080173a83f98e","project_ids":["roanoke-s4"],"server":{"harvested_at":"2026-10-02T13:43:57Z","id":"850779382791536640","name":"Empire City."},"server_slug":"empire-city"}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"854829166561067029","content":"This stall is run by a large bugbear man who talks in extremely dramatic fashion. Many of his pieces of armor are fancy and catching to the eye. He ages his whole lifespan over the course of a day, his taste and required gifts changing with him. The interior of the stall, which is an open-air blacksmithy with a small room in the back for sleeping, has several clocks strewn about. As the day progresses, the bugbear man will go by different variants of the same name: JJ, Jimmy, John, James, and Johnathan. Information on the items sold here can be found in the ferrytown burrough channel. Unlike many of the other shops in Ferrytown which take on a different tone and goods during the night, this shop is instead closed as the bugbear begins to die at sunset and is reborn and ages enough to manage the shop by sunrise.\n\nAll items are made of Fae'd Oak- Weapons or Armor made from this wyld wood have no metal within them, but are just as sturdy as their metal counterparts. Armor made from this Fae'd Oak gives resistance to Psychic and Force Damage. Weapons carved from Fae'd Oak are much less common, mainly because of their instability, when you Crit with these weapons roll on the Fae'd Oak wild magic table:","created_at":"2021-06-17T05:08:02.790000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"854950497391345666","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"854829166561067029","content":"1- Sap pours from the palm of your hands and hardens around whatever weapon you are wielding. For the next 10 minutes the weapon deals an extra damage die of force damage on the first attack that hits and you cannot be disarmed and not use whatever hand or hands are stuck to the weapon.\n2- The latent Fae magic in the weapon surges from within it and into you, revitalizing your stamina. You can roll a d6+2 or a d8+2 and gain that number of hit points or temporary hit points, respectively.\n3- A flumph appears in an empty location of your choosing within 30 feet of you. It, startled at both the sudden atomization and deatomization, uses its Stench Spray ability and disappears at the start of your next turn.\n4- Large vines and roots grow out of the weapon, wrapping around you, and planting themselves into the ground surrounding you. For the next minute or until you take 20 damage the ground 10 feet within you becomes difficult terrain, you gain +2 AC, and resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.\n5- You strike with impeccable flourish, alluring nearby enemies. Up to 3 hostile creatures within 30 feet of you must succeed on a wisdom saving throw, DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your charisma modifier, or become charmed for 10 minutes.\n6- The wrath of the seasons lash out from the weapon. All enemies within 15 feet of you take 1d6 fire damage, 1d6 cold damage, are pushed back 5 feet, and have their speed reduced to zero until your next turn.\n7- The strong force of your strike summons a benevolent nature spirit. The spirit has the statistics of an Awakened Tree, except it is a small fae instead of a huge plant. It takes its turn immediately after yours and can be commanded (no action required). It remains for 10 minutes before returning to the feywild.\n8- The frigid clutch of the Unseelie court blesses you. Armor of Agathys is cast on you at second level, and lasts for the next 10 minutes.","created_at":"2021-06-17T05:08:57.266000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"854950725879332884","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"854829166561067029","content":"ITEMS AVAILABLE:\n**Barkskin Armor**: uncommon, breastplate 3,000g\nYour Armor Class can't be lower than 16 while you wear this armor. It smells of sweet maple.\n\n**Stable breastplate:** uncommon, breastplate, requires attunement 3,000g\nThe first time each day you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, this armor immediately stabilizes you at 1 hp, though you are not conscious.\n\n**Circlet of the suave:** unncommon, wonderous item 2,000g\nthis circlet gives you advantage on saving throws against being charmed or put to sleep\n\n**Two-faced Helmet:** rare, wonderous item, requires attunement, 3,000g\nWhile wearing this helmet, you gain a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your wisdom modifier (minimum of 1) and cannot be surprised unless you are blinded.\n\n**Stoneskin Armor**: rare, armor (plate), 3,500g\nYou have resistance to non-magical bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage while you wear this armor. It smells of rock candy.\n\n**Coward's boots: **uncommon, wonderous item, 2,500g\nWhen you take the disengage action on your turn, your walking speed increases by 10 feet until the end of your turn.\n\n**Viscous armor:** rare, armor (splint), requires attunement, 4,500g\nwhen an enemy rolls a natural 1 to hit you with a melee attack, they must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or have their weapon stick to you. The weapon can be removed by using an action to make a successful DC 15 Strength check. If you were hit with an appendage, the creature is grappled by you instead of being disarmed.","created_at":"2021-07-05T22:19:05.722000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T08:30:01.461000Z","id":"861732950915416096","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"854829166561067029","content":"**Shatterheart Breastplate:** uncommon, armor (breastplate), requires attunement, 1,500g\nWhile wearing this breastplate, if you would be killed due to a blow/attack, instead the armor takes the hit for you and is destroyed, infusing you with enough life essence to be conscious at 1HP, albeit without armor","created_at":"2021-07-05T22:19:09.156000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-05T22:20:08.470000Z","id":"861732965317869568","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
